{
  "id": "pokemon-center-card-battle-2009-2010",
  "name": "Pokémon Center Card Battle 2009-2010",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Center Card Battle (ポケモンセンター カードバトル) was a run of small free tournaments for 30-card decks of the DP series onwards, for elementary school children and younger who knew the rules, first come first served, with decks to borrow. The Pokémon Centers in Osaka, Nagoya, Fukuoka, Yokohama and Sapporo held them in November 2009, and the Centers in Sapporo, Tokyo, Yokohama, Nagoya, Osaka and Fukuoka again in February and March 2010.\n\nIts prizes were six cards with the Pokémon Center logo, Chikorita, Cyndaquil, Totodile, Mareep, Phanpy and Teddiursa, 034 to 039/L-P. In March 2010 every player got one of the six, three straight wins brought another as the excellence prize, and a single win a sticker; the card could not be chosen.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokeboon: ポケモンセンター各店「カードバトル」【2010年】",
